    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you serve Highland?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We're in Pleasant Grove and Highland is a short drive — estimates are free and we don't add travel to the price.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does it cost to replace a driveway in Highland?",
            "answer": "<p>The two things that move the number most are square footage and how much old concrete has to come out. Highland driveways are often longer than average, so it's worth getting a real figure rather than a rule of thumb — the <a href=\"/pages/estimate\">estimator</a> gives you a ballpark and the site visit gives you the price.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you pour a pad for an RV or a toy hauler?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, and it's built differently from a driveway — deeper base, reinforcement, and extra thickness where the jacks and tires sit. Measure your rig and add room to open the door and put the awning out; we'll help size it on site.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long before I can drive on it?",
            "answer": "<p>You can usually walk on it the next day. We ask you to keep vehicles off for about a week while it gains strength, and heavy vehicles longer — we'll give you exact dates for your pour before we leave the site.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
